# The vendored MADiE decks are HASHED, byte for byte, by `measures/official/<id>/manifest.json`'s
# `tests.sha256`, and the gate recomputes that hash from the checked-out bytes. Any line-ending
# translation — `core.autocrlf` on a Windows clone, a future `text=auto` here — would therefore make
# the hash platform-dependent: green on the machine that vendored the deck, red on CI. Marking the
# decks binary is what makes "the bytes CMS published" mean the same thing on every checkout.
backend-ts/measures/official/*/tests/** -text
